    "443" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A code from the web console's API Tokens page fills in the address and signs you in. Typing the address above and entering a token by hand works just as well." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A forward record is created in this zone, and a reverse record if one is configured." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A host name or IP address, plus a port if your control plane isn't on 443. Name it if you like — \"Lab\", \"Prod EU\"." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A host name or IP address. Add a port if your control plane doesn't use 443." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A host name or IP address. Add a port if your control plane doesn't use 443. The name is yours — \"Lab\", \"Prod EU\" — and is what the app calls this server from then on." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A magic packet goes to %@, %@." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A magic packet only reaches the broadcast domain it is sent into, so a machine on another subnet needs its broadcast address here." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A passcode is weaker than biometrics here, and unlike a biometric enrolment it doesn't invalidate the stored token when it changes. Sign in again after setting up biometrics to upgrade this." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A record needs a value." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A record's type can't be changed — an A that becomes a CNAME is a different record." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A token is never stored unprotected. Set a device passcode — and biometrics if this device has them — then come back." : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value"
    },
    "A token is only stored behind a biometric lock. Set up biometrics and a device passcode to continue." : {
